{"type":"message","id":"399fc836","parentId":"952c0cfd","timestamp":"2026-05-27T08:19:42.372Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see that the test `check_unused_fragments_silent_when_fragment_is_used` uses `{{> note }}` syntax (Handlebars-like), while the parser uses `{> note <}` syntax. The plan says to replace `FRAGMENT_INCLUDE_RE` with the parser - but the test uses `{{> note }}` syntax which the parser wouldn't understand.\n\nActually, looking at the step plan more carefully:\n> For fragment detection in `unused_fragment.rs`, parse each source file and collect `Node::Fragment` values.\n\nBut `Node::Fragment` is the `{> name <}` syntax (the parser's syntax), not `{{> name }}`. If I switch `unused_fragment.rs` to use the parser, the existing test would fail because it uses `{{> note }}` which won't produce a `Node::Fragment`.\n \nI need to check what syntax the build system actually uses for fragments in production. Let me look at the build tests to see what format they're working with.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01MzNufE3VdEznZ6Q65dvGXM","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"fragment\\|{>\" X:/repo/skillet/.worktrees/goal-move-the-lint-pipelines-p-mpnrlu69-qmv6ab/crates/skillet-cli/tests/build_tests.rs | head -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"github-copilot","model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","usage":{"input":1,"output":387,"cacheRead":36526,"cacheWrite":669,"totalTokens":37583,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779869969304,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_01A5gJfnV4LmiAyzesLGixpd"}}
