{"type":"message","id":"429b8fa2","parentId":"053754d4","timestamp":"2026-05-27T08:19:56.794Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The production syntax is `{{> note }}` (Handlebars-like), not `{> note <}` (the parser's syntax). These are different syntaxes:\n- `{{> name }}` - Handlebars template include (what the build system uses)\n- `{> name <}` - PanParse fragment syntax\n\nSo the `FRAGMENT_INCLUDE_RE` regex which matches `{{> name }}` is the correct production regex, and it's different from what the parser handles. The plan says to replace with the parser, but the parser uses a completely different fragment syntax!\n\nLooking at the plan step:\n\n\n> For fragment detection in `unused_fragment.rs`, parse each source file and collect `Node::Fragment` values.\n\nThis seems to be based on a misunderstanding - the `Node::Fragment` in the parser corresponds to `{> ... <}` syntax, not `{{> ... }}` syntax. If I switch to the parser, the existing test (which uses `{{> note }}`) would break. And re-reading the evaluator feedback, none of the acceptance tests specifically test the `unused_fragment.rs` changes with the parser syntax - they all already pass.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01X2fwt9FgtiKnLtJLYyQJ5R","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd X:/repo/skillet/.worktrees/goal-move-the-lint-pipelines-p-mpnrlu69-qmv6ab && git log --oneline -10 && echo \"---\" && git show 4703459 --stat | head -10"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"github-copilot","model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","usage":{"input":1,"output":578,"cacheRead":37195,"cacheWrite":750,"totalTokens":38524,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779869982700,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_01UD7dCEFbxxKTZPWnVrcMzd"}}
