{"type":"message","id":"9e9a7c74","parentId":"57c8b84b","timestamp":"2026-05-27T08:21:17.201Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All acceptance criteria pass. The implementation was already committed in round 1. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe implementation was already in place from round 1's commit. All acceptance criteria pass:\n\n**`crates/skillet/Cargo.toml`** — Added `skillet-compiler = { path = \"../skillet-compiler\" }` dependency.\n\n**`crates/skillet-compiler/src/lib.rs`** — Already exposed `pub mod parse` so the parser is accessible cross-crate.\n\n**`crates/skillet-compiler/src/lex.rs` + `parse.rs`** — Already supported `var::` and `env::` ref kinds with full test coverage.\n\n**`crates/skillet/src/refs.rs`** — `ParsedRefs::extract` was rewritten to:\n- Use `PanSource::new` + `PanParse::new` + `parse()` for typed refs and untyped backticks\n- Map parser `RefKind::Reference`/`Path` → `refs::RefKind::Ref`, `Skill`/`Cmd`/`Var`/`Env` directly; skip `Agent`/`Url`\n- Convert `Node::RefSuspect` by slicing source, stripping backticks, and calling `classify_untyped`\n- Continue extracting markdown links via the existing regex\n- Added 7 focused regression tests covering kind mapping, path→Ref, agent/url skipping, untyped classification, unclassifiable ignoring, markdown coexistence, and line/col correctness\n\nAll 145 `skillet` tests and 46 `skillet-compiler` tests pass. The two pre-existing failures in `skillet-cli` build tests are unrelated to this change."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"github-copilot","model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","usage":{"input":1,"output":420,"cacheRead":42210,"cacheWrite":271,"totalTokens":42902,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779870065208,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_019PwRSV4wCrkyu1LbDjMwuo"}}
